# Maintainer batch 20260820-092735. NO ROWS.
#
# Six parked tasks. Five are the closed pre-A23 set. One is a new `r4`.
# No row can release any of them.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. LJ-1.386, LJ-1.388, LJ-1.390, LJ-1.391, LJ-1.395. reason `no-match`.
#
# Unchanged from batch 20260820-082516. Their records predate fact 8, so
# `sys-obligations-satisfied` cannot reach them (`scripts/pod/table.py:563-566`).
# A task-scoped `done` row would pass replay and then rule (a2) would
# re-dispatch them (`scripts/pod/pod.py:3125-3134`). The owner raised
# `parked_max` to 12 instead of closing them in place.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. LJ-1.396. reason `r4`. THIS IS THE NEW INPUT.
#
# Owner `--retry` at seq 169. Coder returned. The record is corpus `c-179` /
# transition seq 179:
#
#   exit 42, error_class unsolved_meta, obligations_delta 0, obligations_open 2
#   conjuncts 1 FAILED, 2-5 held, 6 FAILED
#   row `task-lj-1-396-no-go-stated` (done, outcome no-go)
#
# R4 for `no-go` needs conjuncts 5 and 6 (`scripts/pod/accept.py:313-330`).
# 5 held. 6 failed. The row that matched is the right row: the coder wrote
# `review-of-kappa-is-limit.md` for branch `no-go-stated`, and the report
# states a refutation of `kappa-is-limit`.
#
# MEASURED this batch, why conjunct 6 failed. `precommit_set()` runs
# `check-survey-quotes.py` with cwd = the task worktree
# (`scripts/pod/accept.py:212-225`, `pod.py:3378-3381`). In that tree:
#
#   agents/tasks/LJ-1-396/ holds `lj-1.396-report.md` and
#   `review-of-kappa-is-limit.md`. It does not hold `LJ-1.396.md`.
#
# The checker then prints `LJ-1-396 has no brief` and exits 2
# (`scripts/pod/check-survey-quotes.py:459-464`). The brief exists in the
# MAIN tree and is UNTRACKED (`git status --short` prints `??` for
# `agents/tasks/LJ-1-396/LJ-1.396.md`). A worktree checkout does not carry
# untracked files, so isolation hides the brief from conjunct 6.
#
# A row cannot put that file into the worktree. An `accept` row with the
# same `when` as `no-go-stated` and a lower priority would steal every
# future clean NO-GO close. Re-dispatching now would fail conjunct 6 again.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Expiry fallout. NO ROW. Closed-task rows dying with their tasks, section 4.6.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT WAITS, AND IT IS NOT A ROW.
#
# Conjunct 6 under worktree isolation reads a tree that does not hold an
# untracked brief. That is a program defect. This batch's write scope is the
